  "description": "Subdivision of the existing dwelling to create 2no flats (2x 2-bed) with associated external amenity area, cycle and refuse storage and alteration to the side elevation",
  "epc_number": null,
  "ward": "Longbridge",
  "last_updated": "2026-11-18T11:14:41.897Z",
  "street_name": "GOODEY ROAD",
  "decision_conditions": [
    "&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: rgb(51, 51, 51);&quot;&gt;The proposed development results in the loss of a high-quality family-sized dwellinghouse, the identified need for which is clearly demonstrated in the development plan and supporting evidence base.&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp; Whilst the proposal would create 2x dwellings,&amp;nbsp; these do not meet the London Plan&#x27;s definition of family-sized dwellings and one of the bedrooms would not comply with the&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: rgb(51, 51, 51);&quot;&gt;minimum internal space standards required to ensure adequate quality of accommodation for future occupants&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: rgb(51, 51, 51);&quot;&gt;. As such, the proposal is considered to have a detrimental impact on the borough&#x27;s supply of family housing and is contrary to the following policies: National Planning Policy Framework (August 2026); Policies D6, H9 and T4 of the London Plan (March 2021); and Policies DMD1, DMT1, DMH5, SP3 and SP8, of the Barking and Dagenham Local Plan 2037 (September 2024)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;",
    "&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: rgb(51, 51, 51);&quot;&gt;The proposal fails to meet the required minimum space standards for the double bedroom and built-in storage within the ground floor flat. It would therefore provide a substandard quality of accommodation detrimental to the standard of living of future residents. Therefore, the proposal fails to comply with:&amp;nbsp; National Planning Policy Framework (August 2026); Policy D6 of the London Plan (March 2021);&amp;nbsp; Policy DMH5 of&amp;nbsp; The London Borough of Barking and Dagenham’s Local Plan 2037 (September 2024);&amp;nbsp; and&amp;nbsp; Technical housing standards – nationally described space standard (March 2015)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;",
    "&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: rgb(51, 51, 51);&quot;&gt;The proposed development fails to demonstrate that additional demand for parking from the development could be adequately accommodated in the surrounding area,&amp;nbsp; especially as the application site does not benefit from high levels of access to public transport, and is within the BOM Controlled Parking Zone (CPZ) . The proposal is therefore likely to exacerbate existing parking stress within the CPZ thus add unacceptably to parking stress and congestion in the vicinity of the application site. &amp;nbsp;As such, it fails to comply with the following policies which seek to ensure proposals show how car parking will be designed and managed and to take into consideration on-street parking availability and existing and planned public transport provision:- National Planning Policy Framework (August 2026)- Policies T1, T2, T3, T4, T6 and T6.1 of the London Plan (March 2021)- Policies DMD1, DMT2 and SP8 of the Barking and Dagenham Local Plan 2037 (September 2024)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;"
  ],
